Growth.

66
00:03:34.133 --> 00:03:37.320
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:38.183 --> 00:03:40.868
Visal, how do you feel before exams?

68
00:03:41.983 --> 00:03:45.321
I feel anxiety. My heart beats fast.

69
00:03:46.417 --> 00:03:49.232
That's normal. Stress affects everyone.

70
00:03:50.317 --> 00:03:51.596
What can I do?

71
00:03:52.683 --> 00:03:57.460
Coping strategies help reduce anxiety. Breathing slowly calms the body.

72
00:03:58.550 --> 00:04:01.922
Thanks. I'll also open up to my support network.

73
00:04:03.067 --> 00:04:04.834
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:05.683 --> 00:04:09.366
Grammar focus: Present simple for general truths.

75
00:04:09.666 --> 00:04:10.772
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:11.483 --> 00:04:13.227
Stress affects everyone.

77
00:04:14.117 --> 00:04:16.697
Coping strategies help reduce anxiety.

78
00:04:17.583 --> 00:04:19.293
Sleep improves your mood.

79
00:04:20.233 --> 00:04:25.846
Use the present simple for facts and general truths. Add -s for singular subjects.

80
00:04:26.583 --> 00:04:30.188
Be careful! Don't say: Stress affect everyone.

81
00:04:32.133 --> 00:04:34.342
Say: Stress affects everyone.

82
00:04:34.642 --> 00:04:37.384
Add -s for he, she, it and singular nouns.

83
00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:40.725
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:41.533 --> 00:04:42.860
Caring for the Mind.

85
00:04:43.160 --> 00:04:46.065
Stress affects everyone, especially teenagers.

86
00:04:47.067 --> 00:04:50.947
Building emotional resilience takes practice and a strong support network.

87
00:04:51.933 --> 00:04:54.908
Coping strategies like breathing help manage anxiety.

88
00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:59.804
Opening up and showing self-compassion is not weak; it's brave.

89
00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:03.357
A healthy mindset brings balance and growth.

90
00:05:04.467 --> 00:05:08.503
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:09.350 --> 00:05:10.990
Stress blank everyone.

92
00:05:11.290 --> 00:05:14.931
A, affects. B, affect. C, affecting.

93
00:05:18.467 --> 00:05:20.559
The answer is A: affects.

94
00:05:21.717 --> 00:05:23.960
A feeling of worry or fear is blank.

95
00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:27.739
A, anxiety. B, resilience. C, growth.

96
00:05:31.300 --> 00:05:33.439
The answer is A: anxiety.

97
00:05:34.583 --> 00:05:36.455
Being kind to yourself is blank.

98
00:05:36.755 --> 00:05:42.057
A, self-compassion. B, therapy. C, a mindset.

99
00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:48.145
The answer is A: self-compassion.

100
00:05:49.333 --> 00:05:52.450
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:53.317 --> 00:05:56.141
What coping strategy helps you manage stress?

102
00:06:04.950 --> 00:06:06.508
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:06.808 --> 00:06:14.174
Walking outside helps me manage stress. Fresh air calms my mind, and talking to my best friend always helps.

104
00:06:14.474 --> 00:06:16.207
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:17.117 --> 00:06:22.068
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and present simple for general truths.

106
00:06:22.368 --> 00:06:26.831
Today's value is self-care. Look after yourself and rest when you are sick.

107
00:06:27.131 --> 00:06:29.656
See you in Unit fifteen. Goodbye!

108
00:06:29.956 --> 00:06:33.723
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

